  "body": "This PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change | [Age](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Adoption](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Passing](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) | [Confidence](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [pnpm](https://pnpm.io) ([source](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/tree/HEAD/pnpm/npm/pnpm)) | [`12.20.0` \u2192 `12.21.0`](https://renovatebot.com/diffs/npm/pnpm/12.20.0/12.21.0) | ![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/npm/pnpm/12.21.0?slim=true) | ![adoption](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/adoption/npm/pnpm/12.21.0?slim=true) | ![passing](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/compatibility/npm/pnpm/12.20.0/12.21.0?slim=true) | ![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/npm/pnpm/12.20.0/12.21.0?slim=true) |\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>pnpm/pnpm (pnpm)</summary>\n\n### [`v12.21.0`](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/releases/tag/v12.21.0): pnpm 12.21\n\n[Compare Source](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/compare/v12.20.0...v12.21.0)\n\npnpm 12.21.0 lets `pnpm store add` prepare tarball and git dependencies for offline installs. It also makes repeated installs keep their peer dependency choices and fixes several `lockfile.format: v13`, `nodeLinker: hoisted`, and `pnpm deploy` failures. If a pnpr server refuses a setting, pnpm now resolves locally.\n\n##### Minor Changes\n\n- `pnpm store add` run in a project now prepares downloaded tarballs for every lockfile entry that pins them. Besides registry packages, `pnpm install --offline --frozen-lockfile` can then install dependencies on a tarball URL and dependencies on a git host such as GitHub whose lockfile entry records an `integrity`.\n\n##### Patch Changes\n\n##### Installs that failed\n\n- pnpm now reads a lockfile with a mapping key longer than 1,024 characters written as `'key':`, without the `? ` marker. Before, `pnpm install` and other commands failed on such a lockfile with `ERR_PNPM_BROKEN_LOCKFILE`.\n\n- With `lockfile.format: v13`, `pnpm install` no longer fails to create or rewrite the lockfile when a package declares many of its dependencies as peers.\n\n- Fixed `pnpm deploy` failing with `lockfile.format: v13` when injected workspace packages have hashed peer bindings.\n\n- Frozen installs with v13 lockfiles now accept valid peer dependencies of injected workspace packages that use catalogs.\n\n- Fixed injected workspace packages that depend on themselves linking to a nonexistent directory.\n\n- `pnpm install` with `frozenStore` enabled no longer fails with `ERR_PNPM_FROZEN_STORE_NEEDS_BUILD` when `nodeLinker` is `hoisted`. `pnpm fetch` with `nodeLinker: hoisted` no longer populates global virtual store links or modifies linked agent skills, and it preserves an existing hoisted `node_modules` directory [#&#8203;18037](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/18037).\n\n- A `requirements.txt` beside a `pyproject.toml` that declares `[tool.uv.workspace]` without a `[project]` table no longer makes that directory a Python project. `pnpm install` stopped there with an error when the directory had a `.venv` that pnpm did not create [#&#8203;18023](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/18023).\n\n##### Peer dependencies\n\n- Repeated installs no longer change the peer dependency providers that the previous install chose. This covers adding, updating, or removing a dependency, projects that use different ranges of one dependency, dependency cycles, and injected dependencies with `autoInstallPeers: false` [pnpm/tasks#221](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/221).\n\n  An unchanged install keeps a valid locked peer provider even when a direct dependency provides another compatible version. Explicit `pnpm add` and `pnpm update` requests take precedence over it.\n\n- Workspace projects that select different versions of a peer provider no longer share one copy of the package that depends on it. This affected peers reached through an aliased dependency or a peer dependency cycle.\n\n- A removed dependency no longer comes back as a peer provider. Before, a direct dependency removed with `autoInstallPeers: false` could be restored from an old peer resolution, and a removed one could still supply its old peer context.\n\n- With `nodeLinker: hoisted` and `autoInstallPeers: false`, `pnpm install` no longer creates duplicate copies of a package whose resolved peers are identical. A package also no longer loads a copy of its dependency that was resolved with different peer versions [#&#8203;18003](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/18003).\n\n- `pnpm deploy` now binds optional peers declared only in `peerDependenciesMeta` for linked workspace packages. The deployed manifest and lockfile also retain these peers when filtering dependency groups.\n\n##### Running scripts\n\n- Scripts now stop when pnpm's process group is killed while they are starting.\n\n- Bin shims in the global virtual store no longer include the hoisted modules directory of the project that installed them [#&#8203;18035](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/18035).\n\n- `pnpm pipeline` now rebuilds local packages and reruns build scripts after it restores a shared Cargo build cache with Cargo 1.100 or newer. Before, a worktree could reuse build-script output from the worktree that created the cache.\n\n##### pnpr\n\n- If the pnpr server refuses a setting the install uses, or cannot return the lockfile format pnpm reads, `pnpm install` and `pnpm update` print a warning and resolve locally. Cargo and Python resolution also fall back to resolving locally. pnpm now rejects a pnpr resolution of npm dependencies that does not name its lockfile format.\n\n- `pnpm install` with `pnprServer` now limits the size of the server's resolve and lockfile verification responses. An oversized response ends the request with an error.\n\n- pnpm now displays pnpr error codes and reasons when remote requests fail.\n\n##### Other commands and settings\n\n- `pnpm setup` and the install script now support PowerShell as the login shell on Linux and macOS. They add `PNPM_HOME` to `PATH` in `profile.ps1` under `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/powershell` or `~/.config/powershell` [#&#8203;18026](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/pnpm/issues/18026).\n\n- A `lockfileDir` setting that points at the default lockfile directory now installs the same way as leaving it unset [pnpm/tasks#275](https://redirect.github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/275).\n\n<!-- sponsors -->\n\n#### Platinum Sponsors\n\n<table>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td align=\"center\" valign=\"middle\">\n        <a href=\"https://bit.cloud/?utm_source=pnpm&utm_medium=release_notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/bit.svg\" width=\"80\" alt=\"Bit\"></a>\n      </td>\n      <td align=\"center\" valign=\"middle\">\n        <a href=\"https://openai.com/?utm_source=pnpm&utm_medium=release_notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n          <picture>\n            <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/openai_dark.svg\" />\n            <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/openai_light.svg\" />\n            <img src=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/openai_dark.svg\" width=\"160\" alt=\"OpenAI\" />\n          </picture>\n        </a>\n      </td>\n      <td align=\"center\" valign=\"middle\">\n        <a href=\"https://notion.com/?utm_source=pnpm&utm_medium=release_notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n          <picture>\n            <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/notion.svg\" />\n            <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/notion_light.svg\" />\n            <img src=\"https://pnpm.io/img/users/notion.svg\" width=\